marta-docs: Quick sync: we're getting multiple PR comments about ambiguity in the function-calling vs tool-calling guidance for nested structured outputs. Request: add a short explainer, two canonical envelope examples, SDK normalization snippet, and a migration checklist.

ravi-ml: Agreed. Problem we see: teams use tool-calling to return rich objects, then clients try to call functions on those objects and parsing breaks. Docs should show when to prefer function-calling (clear typed args, small payloads) vs tool-calling (large blobs, third-party tool output).

oliver-sdk: I'll add a small helper that validates against a JSON Schema and falls back to a permissive parser. Draft Python + TS example for the docs: Python snippet:

```python
import json
from jsonschema import validate, ValidationError

SCHEMA = {"type": "object", "properties": {"title": {"type":"string"}, "items": {"type":"array"}} , "required": ["title"]}

def parse_and_validate(raw: str):
    obj = json.loads(raw)
    try:
        validate(instance=obj, schema=SCHEMA)
        return obj
    except ValidationError:
        # permissive fallback: try lenient parse/coerce
        return {"title": str(obj.get("title", "")), "items": obj.get("items", [])}
```

TypeScript sketch:

```ts
import Ajv from 'ajv'
const ajv = new Ajv()
const schema = { type: 'object', properties: { title: { type: 'string' }, items: { type: 'array' } }, required: ['title'] }
const validate = ajv.compile(schema)

export function parseAndValidate(raw: string) {
  const obj = JSON.parse(raw)
  if (validate(obj)) return obj
  return { title: String(obj?.title ?? ''), items: obj?.items ?? [] }
}
```

sophia-eng: Add two canonical envelopes in docs: 1) function-call schema (typed args) example: `{ "name": "summarize", "arguments": { "text": "...", "max_lines": 5 } }` and 2) tool-call envelope for rich content: `{ "tool_output": { "meta": {...}, "payload": { "title": "...", "items": [...] } } }`. Explain that tool_call payloads should include a small "meta" block with content-type and schema-version to help clients validate.

amy-qa: I'll add tests and a cURL example showing both flows. For migration checklist include: update docs link, bump SDK to include parseAndValidate helper, run integration tests against representative tool outputs, and add a telemetry toggle so teams can see how many fallbacks are triggered.

marta-docs: Also fix two stale links in the structured-output page that reference the old "toolcaller" doc. I'll update them to point to /docs/function-calling and /docs/tool-calling-patterns. Will include the preview link in the PR.

